From: openEuler RISC-V Maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tests: link display test to Qt Widgets

License: LGPL-3.0-or-later
Upstream-Status: downstream-only
Origin: openEuler RISC-V packaging

Qt's QTEST_MAIN macro creates a QGuiApplication unless the test target is
compiled with Qt Widgets support.  The display test loads the Trayicon backend,
which explicitly requires QApplication, but its target currently links only
Qt Test and libsnore.  Link Qt Widgets to this target so QTEST_MAIN creates the
application class required by the backend while preserving the complete test.

Remove this patch when upstream links display_test to Qt Widgets or otherwise
constructs QApplication for the test.

---
 autotest/CMakeLists.txt | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/autotest/CMakeLists.txt b/autotest/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/autotest/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/autotest/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -15 +15,2 @@
 ecm_add_tests( snorebenchmark.cpp display_test.cpp LINK_LIBRARIES Snore::Libsnore Qt5::Test)
+target_link_libraries(display_test Qt5::Widgets)
